  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1978-p24.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The three expressions have sum \\[ \\begin{aligned} &x(y-z)+y(z-x)\\\\ &\\qquad+z(x-y)=0. \\end{aligned} \\] Writing the nonzero geometric progression as \\(u,\\) \\(ur,\\) \\(ur^2\\) gives \\(u(1+r+r^2)=0.\\) Since \\(u\\ne0,\\) \\(r^2+r+1=0.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Add the three given expressions",
        "Write the three nonzero terms as \\(u,\\) \\(ur,\\) \\(ur^2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
